9219548,2024-06-10,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"Subject : Continued Inaccuracies in Credit Reporting - Request for Immediate Removal of Inaccurate Account To Whom It May Concern, I am writing to formally file a complaint against the credit bureaus for their continued failure to correct and remove inaccurate information regarding the following account on my credit report : Account Name : XXXX Despite multiple disputes filed under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), the credit bureaus persist in reporting inaccuracies related to this account. Specifically, the following inaccuracies remain : Incorrect status Incorrect reporting Incorrect balance This situation violates several provisions of the FCRA. I request the credit bureaus to permanently remove this account from my credit report due to the failure to validate the charges properly during their investigation. 

Violations and Relevant Laws 15 U.S. Code 1681e ( b ) : Accuracy of Report Consumer reporting agencies must follow reasonable procedures to assure maximum possible accuracy of the information. Despite my dispute, the credit bureaus continue to report inaccuracies, which is grounds for deletion.

